ft README.md` prints a number greater than 0 and expect the same count from docs/INSTALL.md.\n5. The check mutates nothing: uv.lock is byte-identical before and after a run; expect exit 0 from `git diff --quiet uv.lock`.\nGATE ARM: Run `bash scripts/audit-deps.sh`; expect the vulnerability mode still works and the drift mode's compared and behind counts printed.\n","capability_tags":[],"complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-21T01:04:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T03:58:54Z","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"75c094b91ef8bd5837a7c4f94887c87d7ec4fcb9","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","completed_at":null,"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/lore-SUP-DEPS-LORE-20261121","branch":"wt/SUP-DEPS-LORE-20261121","worker_summary":"Merge cab3e6e of wt/SUP-DEPS-LORE-20261121 (worker commit 42dea78, cx/gpt-6.1-terra@9router). scripts/dep-drift.sh: report-only lock-vs-PyPI sweep (tomllib + PyPI GET, no writes); live report 2 of 34 locked packages behind (certifi 2026.10.23->2026.11.20, platformdirs 4.14.7->4.14.8), uv.lock sha256 9b99cbec... unchanged by a run. lore-dep-drift.timer+service armed on this host (next elapse Mon 2026-11-23 07:45); units byte-identical to repo copies in deploy/systemd/; post-merge service start exit 0 with real report appended to ~/.local/share/lore/dep-drift.log (worker's pre-merge 203/EXEC resolved by landing the script at the documented path). README.md + docs/INSTALL.md document the arrangement. Gates on graded tree 75c094b91ef8bd5837a7c4f94887c87d7ec4fcb9: 572 passed, ruff clean, format clean, count guard PASS. Tier-2 verdict PASS/COMPLETE, history run 2026-11-21/09a05b2d (stdout id 779d3d7d).","foreman_note":null,"type":null}
 {"id":"INFRA-LORE-044","title":"[P4] Guard hook budget defaults below its own test timeout — every commit carries a fail-open warning","status":"pending","priority":"P4","created_by":null,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-21 on main 8ec0c83: every commit prints 'WARN: hook_timeout=300s <= test_timeout=1200s in /home/kara/get-h3/lore: the guard would be cut off mid-run and report a fail-open PASS. Raising this run's budget to 1320s'. The repo declares evaluator.test_timeout 600 (.gitreins/config.yaml line 40) but declares no guards.hook_timeout, so the hook budget falls back to a 300s default while the guard itself computes a 1200s effective test timeout. The guard works around it per run, which means the warning is perpetual and the declared-vs-effective gap is never closed: a slow box can still end the hook before the test lane finishes and the commit then reads PASS on a run that never completed. Pre-existing; not caused by any 2026-11-20/21 change. Fix is config-only: declare a hook timeout above the effective test timeout so the guard's own arithmetic stops warning.","detail":{"fingerprint":"a2a18c49ae0ba247461cc310b94c412b936defac7320462570f9e726a1d2a180"},"source":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. The guard's hook budget is declared rather than defaulted: `git grep -c hook_timeout .gitreins/config.yaml` prints a number greater than 0; expect the declared value to exceed the effective test timeout the guard reports.\n2. A board-only commit's guard log carries no fail-open warning: commit a board-only change and expect no line pairing hook_timeout with a smaller number than test_timeout.\n3. Declared and effective test timeouts agree: the guard log's reported test timeout equals the value declared in the config; expect one number, never two.\n4. The guard still reaches a real verdict on a full test run: commit a code change and expect the guard's test lane to report passed tests, not a timeout, at the declared budget.\nGATE ARM: Run `git grep -c hook_timeout .gitreins/config.yaml`; expect a number greater than 0.\n","capability_tags":[],"complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-21T01:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T03:34:17Z","worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"completed_at":null,"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/lore-INFRA-LORE-044","branch":"wt/INFRA-LORE-044","worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"type":null}
